      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 2011, Argyroupoli merged with Elliniko to form the municipality Elliniko–Argyroupoli under Greece's local government reform.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elliniko-Argyroupoli",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Argyroupoli sits at the foot of Mount Hymettus, just a short drive from the Saronic Gulf coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nomadlio.com/argyroupoli/city-guide/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mount Hymettus offers popular hiking trails that let residents enjoy panoramic views of Athens and the surrounding countryside.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nomadlio.com/argyroupoli/city-guide/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Nightlife in Argyroupoli is quieter, focusing on cozy local bars and tavernas rather than large clubs.",
